# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for LRPS2 sweeps.
#
# Usage:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=tests/tsan.supp" <harness>
#
# Two categories only.  Anything TSan reports that is not matched here
# is NEW and must be triaged, not added blindly.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# ACCEPTED BY DESIGN - do not "fix" without an architecture decision.
#
# The EE thread writes GS privileged registers (SMODE1/SMODE2, PMODE,
# DISPFB, ...) directly into shared PS2MEM_GS via gsWrite64_page_00 /
# gsWrite64_generic; the GS side reads them at vsync (GSRenderer::Merge,
# GSState::GetVideoMode / isReallyInterlaced, MTGS::MainLoop's vsync
# path).  Inherited from upstream PCSX2, where priv-reg traffic is
# deliberately not ring-serialized.  Accesses are aligned and
# word-sized on the only supported host (x86-64: single mov, no
# tearing); worst case is a one-frame-stale video mode, which matches
# real-hardware semantics - a mode change mid-scanout is "torn" on a
# real PS2 too.  Serializing these through the MTGS ring would be
# invasive, perf-relevant, and upstream-divergent.
race:GSState::GetVideoMode
race:GSState::isReallyInterlaced
race:gsWrite64_generic
race:gsWrite64_page_00
race:MTGS::MainLoop
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRACKED - empty.
#
# Every entry that lived here has been root-caused and fixed:
#
#   - host-transfer vs in-flight draw (WriteImageX -> WritePixel4HH
#     /4HL/8H against DrawRectT/FillBlock): boost_spsc_queue's
#     empty()/size() loaded both cursors relaxed, so
#     GSRasterizerList::IsSynced() established no happens-before and
#     the Sync() gate in InvalidateVideoMem/InvalidateLocalMem could
#     be skipped.  Fixed by making those query helpers acquire.
#
#   - worker vs worker in GSRasterizer::Draw: 'data.pixels =
#     m_pixels.actual' wrote a field of the SHARED job object from
#     every worker slicing the draw, and nothing ever read it back.
#     Fixed by deleting the dead write and the dead field.
#
# The sweep now reports zero WITHOUT any GS-worker suppression.  If a
# GS race appears here again it is a regression, not a known issue -
# add it only with a root cause, never to quiet the run.
